 "region": "Egypt, the Red Sea",
 "_about": "the ship of Hatshepsut's expedition to Punt (the Deir el-Bahari reliefs, about -1470): a long keel-less hull held from sagging by a hogging truss -- a great cable from stern to stem over forked crutches -- the deck beams' ends through the sides, the stern rising and curling forward into a papyrus umbel, a broad sail far wider than it is tall between a yard and a boom, fifteen oars a side, two great steering oars on the quarters and a railed platform at either end. (About 21-25 m and 5 m in the beam: the Min of the Desert reconstruction is 20 m; the rest estimated from the reliefs)",
